{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.72,"content_digest":"6c16aa3f81066bb6dc048cea0cd8625501b2aa32537b5340288b0888ac608a5f","created_at":"2026-08-22T16:36:18+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"0860481bc20e9cbaa1cad7646f9629eae04924d00d56fe5b7dfda206a3aafec3","input_tokens":5597,"latency_ms":31003,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"52e0be8df90bf823490f3e87b6e7f4ba253261fe31d4fc82c6df4ac48a98e913","output_tokens":2390,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:56e3bf103a3035ca28290d3a","meta_principle_id":"meta:engineering-optimization:experiment-model-iteration","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0N584CAA4M5TEQX5KVB1RG7","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle states that engineering progress requires iteration between models, prototypes, tests, and failure analysis. The new principle is a specialization of this iterative-engineering observation: professional process modeling requires iterative dialogue between modeler and system to resolve descriptive gaps, and a conversational BPMN system lacking that capability leaves such gaps unresolved. The direction is from the general design-process principle to the specific modeling-task design rule.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T17:07:53+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0N72WTZDNS3VF5QZJB70PZ5"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T16:36:18+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.75,"content_digest":"f5a4e24bf1191952c95f48cfbdef2731af63ce1844c1a8fed57b323686aa3cf4","created_at":"2026-08-23T06:50:48+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"7223bd1fafcfde789478a12ed6f48726adfec69a18ecd9e56e9e94a1e9e43f82","input_tokens":5762,"latency_ms":31162,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"dd8f2ec7f5147d692ed0d26afc28b98f8c4cd687437d5f739feecc42be27bce9","output_tokens":2425,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:6e8c3462e7db1243070c1dc8","meta_principle_id":"meta:engineering-optimization:verification-validation-uncertainty","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0PP4R8EE6ZCP0G9SS9VBPCQ","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The VVUQ meta-principle distinguishes uncertainty sources; the standard deviation of repeated inferences is bounded to stochastic sampling variability and does not by itself quantify input, parameter, or model-form uncertainty.","relation_type":"bounded_by","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T06:50:48+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"partial","confidence":0.6,"content_digest":"05e13d6ab08e97c1dfd4d33e8d11bce3708db3445f37659b041cf9565db3914e","created_at":"2026-08-23T03:59:38+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"aec7b3daf7040ed5ef73807b4dcad7b39fa5cb02cdfc89a3d0aa91503f4890e6","input_tokens":5757,"latency_ms":33407,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"90fda9cfa2fe08ff712e4f5c6727b5bf2ef47339967799ad07ffded5725ef142","output_tokens":2540,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:9349210e19dd5aa91686c715","meta_principle_id":"meta:foundations:robustness-sensitivity","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0PCB8D49YSWNDCCP46T2RZS","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The empirical finding that the 0-persistence exponent remains robust to added noise in the Rössler system is a concrete instance of the methodological expectation that credible relations should survive plausible perturbations. The meta-principle is general and methodological, while the principle is a specific study-bound robustness result, so the relation is consistent rather than derivational.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T03:59:38+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
